See COPYING for the license terms.


SUPPORTED PROGRAMS

The supported runtime programs are:

    xpilot-ng-sdl       SDL2/OpenGL game client
    xpilot-ng-server    Dedicated game server

SDL is the sole graphical client platform layer. The former native X11
client, client-side replay viewer, and block-map editor are not part of this
source tree. A server-only build remains available.

This cleanup prepares the client architecture for later portability work. It
does not provide a WebAssembly or browser build yet.


NETWORK MODEL

The client connects directly to one server over TCP. Gameplay and short-lived
status or administration requests share the server's fixed `gamePort`, which
defaults to 15345 and is selected with `-port` on both programs. No lobby,
LAN-discovery, or metaserver client is included. If no server argument is
given, xpilot-ng-sdl connects to 127.0.0.1.

This direct TCP topology is an intermediate step toward a future browser
client. It does not add WebSocket, TLS, HTTP asset delivery, or browser-side
runtime support.


BUILDING

Installation instructions and dependencies are documented in INSTALL. The
usual build is:

    ./configure
    make
    make check
    make install

To omit the SDL client and build only the server and shared data, configure
with:

    ./configure --disable-sdl-client

Manual pages for the programs are in doc/man.


CONTRIBUTED SOFTWARE

The contrib directory contains standalone tools that are not part of the
normal build or source distribution. In particular, contrib/jxpmap contains a
separate editor for polygon-based map files.


REPORTING PROBLEMS

When reporting a problem to xpilot-hacks@lists.sourceforge.net, include the version,
platform, build configuration, and enough detail to reproduce the symptom.
